Package: space.kern0x1b.kindlesyncfix
Name: Kindle Whispersync Fix (unofficial)
Architecture: iphoneos-arm
Description: The Kindle app's Whispersync backend now rejects a malformed empty "Expect" HTTP header that old CFNetwork attaches to its sync requests on iOS 6, returning "417 Expectation Failed" and breaking "Sync to Furthest Page". This tweak hooks -[NSMutableURLRequest setValue:forHTTPHeaderField:] inside the Kindle app only, and drops the header when its value is empty, restoring sync. It writes no logs and stores no data. Unofficial and independent: not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Amazon.com, Inc. Amazon, Kindle and Whispersync are trademarks of Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates.
Maintainer: kern0x1b
Author: kern0x1b
Section: Tweaks
Tag: purpose::extension
Homepage: https://github.com/kern0x1b/kindle-sync-fix
Depiction: https://kern0x1b.github.io/cydia/depictions/kindlesyncfix.html
Icon: https://kern0x1b.github.io/cydia/icons/kindlesyncfix.png
Depends: mobilesubstrate
Provides: space.kern0x1b.expectfix
Replaces: space.kern0x1b.expectfix
Conflicts: space.kern0x1b.expectfix
